      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, you have hit on the core criticism: the primary engines of international law and humanitarian action are often the \"least important interests of the biggest powers.\" When the balance of power wavers, no one has enough leverage to silence the narrative that international law is being \"abused\" or \"ignored\" in the real world. While these organizations take their \"stiff upper lip,\" the guarantee of what is right for a country is often more political than moral.",
